because a multi-selection summary is an aggregate that nothing can decompose. Everything
else is yours:

38afedd162c468a49b3d68d0.source:
Opens the data dock — the graph's rows as a sortable, selectable grid split off
the bottom of the canvas. `full` mode only, and only when `UI.table` allows it;
a no-op otherwise.

14d752915037e5c8eed4012e.source:
Builds this mode's flyout panel. Required for `kind: 'flyout'` and ignored
otherwise. The panel is mounted into the flyout slot and torn down with the mode;
the subclass's own `mode` must equal this definition's [id](#id).

a9f3970941c8c7b21c2f3775.source:
`'default'` is the tool a mode rests on when nothing special is armed (Select's
Pointer); `'toggle'` arms a modal tool and morphs the rail slot to match it;
`'action'` runs once and leaves the armed tool alone.

6dc54155a2520dd7d71a3417.source:
`'ingested'` an auto-ingest pivot landed its results; `'staged'` candidates
are waiting in triage; `'refused'` the cap or the ceiling turned it away;
`'vetoed'` `onBeforeIngest` refused it; `'failed'` the provider threw;
`'cancelled'` the run was superseded or abandoned before it landed.

